{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSCj4XUVkrYQSEggBJbN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it so a `save_fact` no longer changes any cached bytes, but I haven't tested it against the real API. I wrote up the changes and which parts of the note applied in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Why the note's fix alone wouldn't work here:** the note's main fix is two cache markers, one on the instructions and one on the per-user part. On this bot, the first marker would almost certainly be ignored. The log shows user 77's whole prefix cached at exactly **1024 tokens**, which is the smallest prefix Claude Sonnet 4.5 will cache. Each fact adds about 15 tokens, so the tools plus instructions come to only about 900. The API silently skips caching a segment that small, and every `save_fact` would still rebuild about 1050 tokens. The colleague's version probably worked because they had about 55 tool definitions in front of their instructions; this bot sends only 2 by default.\n\n**What I changed in `bot.py`:**\n- **New facts no longer touch the cached part.** The cached per-athlete block lists only the facts saved before the current cache was created. Facts saved since then go in a small block at the end with no cache marker, costing about 15 tokens per fact at full price. The model still sees every fact, so it still won't save one twice.\n- **Recent facts move into the cached block only when the cache has expired anyway:** no call in the last 5 minutes, or a new day. Two new fields on the athlete record track this (`cached_facts` and `last_call`). Existing records without them still load fine.\n- **The system prompt is built once per message.** Before, a `save_fact` in round 1 changed the prompt for round 2 of the same answer. That's where the misses in `logs/usage.jsonl` come from.\n- I kept the two markers. The first one only helps when a planning or race tool is added, which makes the prefix big enough to cache; otherwise it's ignored at no cost.\n\n**Testing:** the Anthropic SDK isn't installed here, and I made no API calls. I ran a simulation with a fake API through three messages, one with a `save_fact`. The cached blocks were byte-identical across all four calls, and the new fact appeared in the uncached end block. After a faked 6-minute gap, the fact moved into the cached block. To check it for real: within 5 minutes, send a message, then one that saves a fact, then one more. The calls after the save should show `cache_creation_input_tokens: 0` and a cache read of about 1050 tokens.\n\n**Not changed:** I left the keyword-based tool filtering in place, as `NOTES.md` asks. It still causes a full cache miss whenever a message adds the planning or race tools (the 1305 and 1334-token rebuilds in the log). Sending all tools every time would remove those misses, but that's your call.\n\nI also updated the caching paragraph in `README.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":133,"cache_read_input_tokens":45556,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":133},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e91d63e-97a6-4324-97dc-c0a218cf6738","uuid":"871a4877-4680-4abc-81b9-819b7bf9ae6a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:38:38.818Z","request_id":"req_011CgSCj4HqXvMX6d8ZoT6hY"}
